        "4330": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes from file B at its pointer into memory at HL in RAM bank C (DOS_JUMPS $0112).\nThe pointer moves on by the bytes read; reading stops at the file's length, after the bytes\nbefore it are read.\nEntry: B = the file number, C = the bank, HL = the address, DE = the count.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear, A = the error ($19 at the length, $1D not open for\nreading, or a disk error) and DE = the bytes not read.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; $DFD0-$DFD2.","comment":"$DFD0 = the bank to fill"},
